<title>GERMANY: German March 1997 metals output detailed.</title>
<headline>German March 1997 metals output detailed.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>German copper and lead output rose in Jan/March 1997 while zinc and aluminium output was lower than in the same 1996 period, official figures showed on Friday.</p>
<p>Base metals data from the state statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) showed output of semi-finished non-ferrous metals products in the three months was higher than a year earlier.</p>
<p>Castings figures were lower apart from aluminium.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes --</p>
<p>METALS OUTPUT	March 97 Jan/March 97  Cumulative pct change</p>
<p>							    over Jan/March 96</p>
<p>primary aluminium	47,958  140,598		  -  3.7</p>
<p>electrolytic copper    51,157  148,388		  +  2.4</p>
<p>zinc			 27,524   77,430		  -  5.5</p>
<p>refined lead	     19,097   53,953		  + 17.6</p>
<p>SEMI-FINISHED MTLS March 97 Jan/March 97  Pct change over 1996</p>
<p>aluminium		 140,910  415,001		  + 11.6</p>
<p>copper		    126,074  383,956		  +  4.8</p>
<p>zinc			 14,705   40,458		  +  5.2</p>
<p>lead			  3,834   11,356		  +  9.1</p>
<p>nickel			1,506    4,923		  + 10.3</p>
<p>METALS CASTINGS    March 97  Jan/March 97 Pct change over 1996</p>
<p>aluminium		  42,870   131,310		 +  2.1</p>
<p>copper			6,244    19,428		 -  3.1</p>
<p>zinc			  5,187    16,123		 -  2.7</p>
<p>lead			    457     1,443		 - 20.5</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures included alloys. Nickel and tin castings data were not given.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
